---
title: Tomato Basil Chicken Fettuccine
description: Quick weeknight fettuccine with seared chicken, burst cherry tomatoes, basil, and butter.
source: https://damndelicious.net/2016/02/02/tomato-basil-chicken-fettuccine/
author: Chungah Rhee (Damn Delicious)
servings: 4
time required: 30 minutes
course: main
cuisine: Italian
tags:
  - chicken
  - pasta
  - tomato
  - basil
  - quick
---

> Adapted from Damn Delicious. Fresh tomatoes and basil are key; leftover chicken works in a pinch.

In a #large pot{} of boiling salted water, cook @fettuccine{8%oz} according to package directions; drain well.

Season @boneless skinless chicken thighs{4} with @Italian seasoning{1%tbsp}, and @kosher salt{} and @black pepper{} to taste.

Heat @olive oil{1%tbsp} in a #large skillet{} over medium-high heat. Add chicken and cook, flipping once, until cooked through, about ~{5-6%minutes} per side. Set aside and keep warm.

Add @garlic{2%cloves}(minced), @cherry tomatoes{2%cups}(halved), @fresh basil{1%cup}(chiffonade), and optional @crushed red pepper flakes{1/2%tsp} to the skillet. Cook, stirring occasionally, until the tomatoes begin to burst and soften, about ~{5%minutes}.

Stir in the pasta and @unsalted butter{1/2%cup} until melted and well combined, about ~{2%minutes}. Season with salt and pepper to taste.

Serve immediately, topped with the sliced chicken and @Parmesan cheese{1/4%cup}(freshly grated).
